WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.069
The bill prevents any government

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.959
institution from infringing on the

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.579
fundamental rights of a parent to

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.188
direct the upbringing, education,

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:10.799
health care and mental health

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.059
of a child.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:12.959
"It is a fundamental right of

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.519
parents to direct the upbringing,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.019
education and care of their minor

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.029
children." That's the opening line

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.289
of Florida's Parent's Bill of

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.149
Rights, signed into law in June

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.439
2021.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.089
Similar bills have been proposed in

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.979
Missouri, Kentucky, Texas and

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.569
even at the federal level.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.489
Our children do not belong to

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.449
the government.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.679
Patty Sullivan is the state

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.029
coordinator for Parental Rights

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.319
Florida, which has pushed for a

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.569
parent's bill of Rights since 2013.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.519
We do not co-parent with

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.409
the government, and these

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.359
entities seem to think

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.429
that they are entitled

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.349
to our children and they are

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:46.829
not.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.419
State bans on the teaching of

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.799
critical race theory, which have

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.299
swept the nation, are also an

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.249
attempt to limit the discretion

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.689
that teachers and administrators

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.989
have over what's taught in school.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.589
They've been especially popular with

00:00:58.590 --> 00:00:59.639
voters.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.469
Republican Glenn Youngkin ousted

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.269
the heavily favored Terry McAuliffe

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.738
in the Virginia governor's race

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:06.569
after he campaigned against

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.549
critical race theory in schools

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.049
and on his first day in office.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.089
He banned it from classrooms via

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.379
executive order.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.909
Four other states have also banned

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:15.839
CRT.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.609
Several more are considering similar

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.579
bills. However, opponents

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.359
say that curriculum transparency

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.369
bills are just thinly veiled

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:25.289
attempts at chilling teachers

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:26.729
and students from learning and

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.379
talking about race and gender in

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.429
schools.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.649
As the ACLU recently tweeted,

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.239
parents have never had the right to

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.069
shape their kids' school curriculum.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.899
Authors of a recent Washington Post

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.089
op ed argued If that's what parents

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.889
want, they should opt out and send

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.059
their children to private or

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.229
religious schools.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.399
But why should families who can

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.899
afford private school be the only

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.219
ones who have a say in what their

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.359
children are taught?

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.099
I'm pretty skeptical of the

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.869
government deciding what should be

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.149
taught in any type of school.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.659
Corey DeAngelis is the national

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:55.769
director of research for the

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.779
American Federation for Children and

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.279
a senior fellow at the Reason

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.239
Foundation.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.129
He says public school parents should

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.329
also have the right to choose the

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.709
right academic setting for their

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.779
kids. The solution is to fund

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.879
students, not systems, giving

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.529
families the choice to spend

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.149
education dollars on the schooling

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.979
of their choosing instead of the

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.749
one size fits all approach offered

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.489
by traditional public schools.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.589
These bills are just a form of whack

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.599
a mole where your CRT battles

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.549
of today were the common

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.469
core battles of yesterday,

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.599
and it'll be something else

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.639
going forward because the reality

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.519
is parents disagree

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.379
about what kind of education

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.579
they want their kids to have.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.919
Families have different preferences,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.749
risk tolerance levels

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.849
and desires for their kids education

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.439
and how they want their kids raised.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.789
And that's OK.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.589
And the better solution is the

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.359
bottom up accountability, allowing

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.739
families to vote with their feet.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.349
Obviously, they can seek an

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.149
education provider that aligns with

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:54.779
their values.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.219
This has become such a hot button

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.719
issue because the pandemic gave

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.999
parents direct exposure to exactly

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.619
what their children were and weren't

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.399
being taught.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.079
Parents are awake now that they have

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.399
seen the curriculum that's been

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.809
streamed into their living room as

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.339
they watch their children do these

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.179
school assignments.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.129
Tina Descovich is a former Provide

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.719
County Florida school board member

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.609
and co-founder of Moms for Liberty.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.349
They now understand school district

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.579
policies, which they have never

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.539
looked at before. They are

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.979
understanding the structure and who

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.359
holds authority and what types of

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.279
authority within the education

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.109
system. I think that's vital, and

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:25.949
it's something that's been lacking

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:26.950
for a long time.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.839
In contrast to critical race theory

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.489
bans, the Florida Parental Bill of

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.589
Rights broadly affirms that parents

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:34.849
have a right to know what schools

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.079
are teaching and providing to their

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:36.889
children.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.119
One of the most controversial

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.499
aspects of the bill is how it

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.879
applies to medical and mental health

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:41.899
services.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.459
It establishes that any medical

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.049
services provided without parental

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.029
consent can result in misdemeanor

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:47.929
charges.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:49.219
Sullivan says some parents are

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.959
particularly concerned that schools

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.249
are counseling their kids on their

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.719
sexuality and gender without

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:54.799
parental consent.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.269
The parents of one student in a

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:58.099
Tallahassee public school sued after

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.509
the staff held a meeting without

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.739
their knowledge to discuss

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.269
accommodating their 13 year old

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.009
shift to a nonbinary gender

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.169
identity. They also noted in a filed

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.969
the students privacy when speaking

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.889
to parents had to be considered.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.209
School districts are not medical

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.429
facilities. That's a complicated

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.709
issue, and there should be

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.898
no reason why parents

00:04:17.899 --> 00:04:19.969
should not be aware of what's going

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:20.929
on with their children.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:22.729
It is a complicated issue.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.679
Where do the rights of parents end

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.419
and the privacy rights of teenagers

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:27.979
who want to confide in a trusted

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.379
teacher or counselor begin?

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:31.999
It was a topic hotly debated on the

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.709
floor of the Florida Legislature

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.479
preceding the passage of the bill.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.189
The bill says that they can be

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.190
fired.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.479
For giving the student

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.699
critical advice

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.759
during their time of need, if

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.779
that advice

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.340
includes,

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.079
maybe you should wait to

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.339
come out to your parents,

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.499
some of our young LGBTQ plus

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.359
kids who are worried that if

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.219
they talk to a teacher or a

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.539
counselor about their gender

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.879
identity or sexual orientation, that

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.409
they're going to be outed to their

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.009
parents,

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.929
we have to provide and

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:10.819
should provide some

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:13.849
confidentiality for those students

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:14.959
to be able to reach

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.169
for a lifeline

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.909
with a trusted educator.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:22.429
The law states that they must

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.679
share all information with a parent.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.739
That's the law.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.509
You don't think that that's a

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.489
problem in terms of, you know,

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:34.369
a teenager having some privacy

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.089
rights.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.949
The when they're

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.809
18, they

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.029
gain those privacy

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:41.809
rights.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.729
And even Fariba makes

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.619
it very clear that it's a parent and

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.509
child relationship that's

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.909
dealing with privacy together.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.889
So I think that

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:54.079
it's very important that we maintain

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.519
the fact that these parents are

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.349
entrusting their children to

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.329
these entities and they

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.269
are not qualified or equipped

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:03.769
to make those decisions.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:05.749
We force families into a one size

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.219
fits all government run school

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.169
system, and these bills try to

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.239
prohibit or encourage

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:12.919
certain types of policies in that

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.459
one size fits all system.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.549
The only way to move forward with

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:18.439
freedom rather than force is

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.579
to allow the money to follow the

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.409
child to wherever they want to

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.209
get an education that aligns best

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.339
with their parents values.

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.079
The pandemic related school closures

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.429
have bolstered the school choice

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.649
movement, with 22 states expanding,

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.719
improving or implementing new school

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.819
choice programs in 2021.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.289
Florida is already far ahead of most

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.399
states and providing parents with

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.109
school choice, but DeAngelis says

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:40.819
this should go farther by offering

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.469
universal vouchers, which would

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:44.719
truly empower parents and children

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.519
to opt for any school of their

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.359
choosing.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.339
Funding students directly truly

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.379
empowers parents when it comes

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:52.519
to their kids education.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.379
That is the best way to assert

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.429
those rights.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.659
Teachers unions have finally

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.219
overplayed their hand, showed their

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.959
true colors and awakened a sleeping

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.819
giant, which happens to be parents

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.079
who want more of a say in their

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.399
kids' education.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.409
At this point, the teachers unions

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:07.999
are actively destroying their own

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.769
empire, and it's actually pretty

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:11.899
glorious. And I'm optimistic going

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.729
forward because parents

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:14.899
have woken up.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.969
Parents felt powerless in 2020,

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:17.989
and they're going to fight to make

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.789
sure they never feel powerless ever

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:20.870
again going forward.

